\barnum returns the bar number currently playing.
When called by itself it does nothing. To print the current
bar, you must call it with \print.

\print \barnum

It can also be used with other commands, like send of an
OSC client, like below:

\myosc.send "/barnum" \barnum

Note that the word "barnum" is used twice in the example
above. Once with a forward slash, which is the OSC
address, and once with a backslash, which is the actual
command.

If no bar has been defined yet, this command returns -1.
